 "answer": "Probably not by much. Tomorrow (17 Oct) is likely to be as bad as today or worse, and relief may only come later.\n\n- **Forecast:** NEA's PSI forecast for 17 Oct 2026 is 150–230 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy). That range reaches higher than the one for today. NEA had forecast Unhealthy to Low Very Unhealthy for 16 Oct.\n- **Latest readings:** As at 8pm, the 24-hr PSI was 159–222, in the Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy range. At 10am today, the central, eastern and western regions were already in the very unhealthy range, at 226, 202 and 201.\n- **Possible improvement:** Some showers are expected tomorrow, and winds should shift to blow from the southeast or south-southeast. That may reduce the transport of smoke haze from Kalimantan to Singapore. Some smoke haze from Sumatra may still drift towards Singapore.\n- **Weekend:** More showers are forecast over Singapore and parts of Kalimantan, and winds are expected to shift to blow from the southeast or south. That makes the weekend look better than tomorrow.\n\n**Advice for tomorrow:**\n- Healthy people should avoid prolonged or strenuous outdoor exertion.\n- The elderly, pregnant women and children should minimise time outdoors.\n- People with chronic lung or heart conditions should avoid outdoor activity.\n- For activities in the next hour, check the 1-hr PM2.5 reading on the NEA site or app. Those readings can change quickly.\n\nHaze forecasts can change quickly with wind and rain, so check NEA's evening update tonight.",
